  "body": "Global development workflow, step G3b, decision 32. Nothing stops work from starting on a half-specified issue. The build loop wants \"every change has a complete issue\", but nothing defines complete or checks it.\n\n## What changes\n\nA `ready` command in the issue tool. It moves an issue to Ready on its board only when the Definition of Ready holds:\n\n- it has its `type:` label, and a `scope:` label if its repository defines any;\n- its body has every section its form requires, with \"done when\" filled in;\n- Priority, Size and Estimate are set, Estimate in hours of agent time;\n- it belongs to a milestone or has a parent issue;\n- nothing it is blocked by is still open;\n- an Architecture-sized issue links to its design in the project note.\n\nOtherwise it refuses and names every unmet item. A build handoff is written only for a Ready issue.\n\n## Done when\n\nAn issue meeting every item moves to Ready, an issue missing any is refused with each missing item named, an issue blocked by an open issue is refused, and Claude's review passes.\n",
